  ],
  "question": {
    "text": "Which of the following arrangements represents the increasing order (smallest to largest) of ionic radii of the given species $\\mathrm{O}^{2-}, \\mathrm{S}^{2-}, \\mathrm{N}^{3-}, \\mathrm{P}^{3-}$ ?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "4i7sQ",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{O}^{2-} < \\mathrm{N}^{3-} < \\mathrm{S}^{2-} < \\mathrm{P}^{3-}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "0nvfR",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{O}^{2-} < \\mathrm{P}^{3-} < \\mathrm{N}^{3-} < \\mathrm{S}^{2-}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "lfe13",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{N}^3 < \\mathrm{O}^{2-} < \\mathrm{P}^{3-} < \\mathrm{S}^{2-}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "0gHpT",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{N}^{3-} < \\mathrm{S}^{2-} < \\mathrm{O}^{2-} < \\mathrm{P}^{3-}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "For isoelectronic species ionic radii decreases as the charge on ion decreases. Further on moving down in a group ionic radii increases. Hence the correct order is $\\mathrm{O}^{2-} < \\mathrm{N}^{3-} < \\mathrm{S}^{2-} < \\mathrm{P}^{3-}$",
    "image": null
  },
